        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Hence write down the equations of the two branches of $y=\\dfrac{|x|}{x}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=\\begin{cases}-1,&x<0,\\\\1,&x>0.\\end{cases}$",
          "worked": "For $x<0$, $|x|=-x$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\frac{-x}{x}\\\\y&=-1.\\end{align*}$$\nFor $x>0$, $|x|=x$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\frac{x}{x}\\\\y&=1.\\end{align*}$$\nThese are the two horizontal branches found in part b; neither includes $x=0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 62
